WEBVTT

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.550
Maybe I should wait
till morning.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:09.593
Like hell.

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:10.594
Pop.

00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:13.847
All together,
we’re 381 years old.

00:00:13.931 --> 00:00:15.557
We don’t wait.

00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:26.401
Now, Charlie, you mustn’t
feel too disappointed.

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:27.819
You know,
if you don’t

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.987
get the...

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.740
Whatever happens,
you’ll still have the candy.

00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:43.335
( foil crinkling )

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.800
( music quietly building )

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.104
Ah, well.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:04.481
That’s that.

00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:08.026
We’ll share it.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.194
Oh, no, Charlie.

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:11.154
Not your birthday present.

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:15.742
It’s my candy bar,
and I’ll do what I want with it.

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.041
Thank you, darling.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.585
Thank you, Charlie.

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:31.508
Thank you.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.770
( inhales deeply )

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:50.610
( dog barking )

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.745
All right,
let’s see who found it.

00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.084
"The third ticket
was found

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.086
by Miss Violet Beauregarde."

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.171
Hah! Hah!

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:10.213
Hah!
( yells )

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:11.131
Hah!

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:12.924
Hah! Huh!

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.009
Hai! Huh!

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:15.052
Hah!
( grunts )

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:16.345
Huh!

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:21.099
( blows bubble, pops )

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.522
These are just some

00:02:27.606 --> 00:02:30.484
of the 263 trophies
and medals

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.444
my Violet has won.

00:02:32.486 --> 00:02:33.904
I’m a gum chewer, mostly,

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:35.989
but when I heard
about these ticket things,

00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:38.325
I laid off the gum,
switched to candy bars.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:40.160
She’s just a driven young woman.

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:41.953
I don’t know where she gets it.

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:45.957
I’m the Junior World
Champion Gum Chewer.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.126
This piece of gum I’m chewing
right at this moment,

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.336
I’ve been working on

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:51.338
for three months solid.

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:52.714
That’s a record.

00:02:52.798 --> 00:02:55.133
Of course, I did have
my share of trophies.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.302
Mostly baton.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:00.597
So it says that one kid’s
going to get this special prize,

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:01.848
better than all the rest.

00:03:01.932 --> 00:03:04.309
I don’t care
who those other four are.

00:03:04.351 --> 00:03:06.353
That kid-- it’s gonna be me.

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:07.729
Tell them why, Violet.

00:03:07.813 --> 00:03:09.981
Because I’m a winner.

00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:12.109
What a beastly girl.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.443
Despicable.

00:03:13.485 --> 00:03:16.488
You don’t know
what we’re talking about.

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:19.658
Dragonflies?

00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:21.910
TV REPORTER:
But wait, this is just in.

00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:24.579
The fourth golden ticket
has been found

00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:28.125
by a boy called Mike Teavee.

00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:33.046
( rapid gunfire )

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.757
( gunfire continues )

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:41.972
All you had to do was track
the manufacturing dates,

00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:43.682
offset by weather

00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:46.351
and the derivative
of the Nikkei Index.

00:03:46.435 --> 00:03:48.603
A retard could figure it out.

00:03:48.687 --> 00:03:49.896
Most of the time,

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.023
I don’t know
what he’s talking about.

00:03:52.107 --> 00:03:53.650
You know, kids these days,

00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:55.444
what with
all the technology.

00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:58.071
Die! Die! Die!

00:03:58.155 --> 00:03:59.197
( gunfire continues )

00:03:59.281 --> 00:04:02.159
Doesn’t seem like
they stay kids very long.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.368
( grunts )

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.245
( gunfire )

00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:06.538
( gunfire stops )

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.458
In the end,
I only had to buy one candy bar.

00:04:09.541 --> 00:04:11.042
And how did it taste?

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.419
I don’t know.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:14.004
I hate chocolate.

00:04:14.045 --> 00:04:16.089
Well, it’s a good thing
you’re going

00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:18.258
to a chocolate factory,
you ungrateful little...

00:04:18.341 --> 00:04:21.219
( no audio )

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.559
( no audio )

00:04:27.642 --> 00:04:29.728
TV REPORTER:
...that question is:

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:32.147
"Who will be the winner
of the last golden...?"

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.191
( turns off TV )

00:04:37.027 --> 00:04:39.029
Dad?

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.113
Yes, Charlie?

00:04:40.197 --> 00:04:41.907
Why aren’t you at work?

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.034
Uh, well,

00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:45.452
uh... toothpaste factory

00:04:45.535 --> 00:04:47.370
thought they’d give me
a bit of time off.

00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:49.456
Like summer vacation?

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:50.707
Sure.

00:04:50.749 --> 00:04:52.751
Something like that.

00:04:55.212 --> 00:04:59.466
NARRATOR:
In fact, it wasn’t
like a vacation at all.

00:04:59.549 --> 00:05:04.137
The upswing in candy sales
had led to a rise in cavities,

00:05:04.221 --> 00:05:08.391
which led to a rise
in toothpaste sales.

00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:11.102
( whirring )

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.606
With the extra money,

00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:16.691
the factory had decided
to modernize,

00:05:16.775 --> 00:05:20.612
eliminating Mr. Bucket’s job.

00:05:20.695 --> 00:05:23.782
( whirring )

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.659
( wind whistling )

00:05:25.742 --> 00:05:27.953
We were barely making
ends meet as it was.

00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:30.372
Oh, you’ll find
another job.

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:32.123
Until then,
I’ll just, um...

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.460
well, I’ll just thin down
the soup a little more.

00:05:35.502 --> 00:05:38.171
Don’t worry, Mr. Bucket.

00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:39.464
Our luck will change.

00:05:39.548 --> 00:05:40.882
Mmm.

00:05:40.966 --> 00:05:43.885
I know it.

00:05:45.512 --> 00:05:48.098
GRANDPA JOE ( whispers ):
Charlie.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.272
( snoring softly )

00:06:03.405 --> 00:06:06.741
My secret hoard.

00:06:08.577 --> 00:06:10.328
You and I

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:15.834
are going to have one more fling
at finding that last ticket.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:18.837
Are you sure you want to spend
your money on that, Grandpa?

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.422
Of course I’m sure.

00:06:20.505 --> 00:06:21.756
Here.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.175
Run down to the
nearest store

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:28.054
and buy the first Wonka
candy bar you see.

00:06:28.138 --> 00:06:33.351
Bring it straight back,
and we’ll open it together.

